{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanTowerConvergence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanTowerConvergence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanMarkovTrace","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.AbsoluteValue.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromean_pair_within_radius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromean_pair_within_radius","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanTowerConvergence.lean#L106-L115","doc":"**The composite convergence bound** (the TRUE bound of the\nformalize-first plan): on the physical domain (`h ≠ 0`, `h² ≤ 1`)\nthe Borromean free-pair argument is inside the Li₂^q radius for\nevery `q > 1`. Together with `pair_trace_dressed_lt_radius` this\ngives convergence of every pair term of the brane tower over the\nBorromean nucleon — for ALL Z, with no per-isotope hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.pair_trace_dressed_lt_radius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.pair_trace_dressed_lt_radius","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanTowerConvergence.lean#L92-L104","doc":"**Interface-dressed pair radius bound.** The bound survives dressing\nby any bond factor with `|f| ≤ 1` (at q₀ the Phase 5q factors are\n`f_pp = f_pn = z ≈ 0.499` and `f_nn = z − h ≈ 0.290`, both in\n`(0,1)`; their membership is a downstream numeric fact). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.pair_trace_lt_radius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.pair_trace_lt_radius","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanTowerConvergence.lean#L82-L90","doc":"**Free-pair radius bound (generic).** Any trace value with `|t| < 1`\nhas its pair argument `t·t` inside the Li₂^q radius `q` for `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.abs_trM_borromean_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.abs_trM_borromean_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanTowerConvergence.lean#L65-L78","doc":"**Two-sided bound on the physical domain.** For `h ≠ 0` with\n`h² ≤ 1` (the substrate has `h₀² ≈ 0.0437`), the trace also stays\nabove `−1`: the numerator plus denominator is `8 + 2h² − 3h⁴ − h⁶ ≥\n8 − 2h² ≥ 6 > 0`. Combined with `trM_borromean_lt_one`, `|t| < 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanTowerConvergence.lean#L52-L63","doc":"**The Borromean trace is strictly below 1 for every `h ≠ 0`.**\nFrom the closed form, `1 − t = (3h⁴ + h⁶)/(h² + 4)` with a positive\nnumerator when `h ≠ 0`. At `h = 0` the trace is exactly 1\n(`isBorromeanMarkovTrace_one_at_zero`), so the hypothesis is sharp. ","signatureChunk":0}]}